WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.822
HTTP describes requests and responses such as GET /notes and a status code.

00:00:05.822 --> 00:00:10.301
HTTPS carries HTTP through a protected connection, typically using TLS.

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:18.810
Encryption protects data in transit, while server identity checks help the browser determine which endpoint it is communicating with.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.292
No.

00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:26.074
HTTPS protects the communication channel; the server must separately check publishing permissions.

00:00:26.074 --> 00:00:31.375
Encrypted delivery of an unauthorised action is still an authorisation failure.

00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:36.685
Which layer of protection does HTTPS primarily provide?

00:00:36.685 --> 00:00:43.150
TLS protects the channel and supports server authentication; application checks remain necessary.
